    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0535" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/765</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs at Nanking to
                        the Chinese Legation</hi><anchor n="74" xml:id="d444-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-16">December 16, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cheng Hsiao-Shu and others of the puppet government in the Three Eastern
                    Provinces planned to set up a monarchy with Pu Yi as emperor in March of next
                    year. The detailed plan as drafted by Cheng contemplated the restoration of the
                    Manchu Dynasty. The Japanese had given their consent to the establishment of the
                    monarchy although they refused to consent to the restoration of the Manchu
                    Dynasty for fear that such a restoration might effect the opinion of the world
                    on Japan.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
